.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt ZCHANGELOG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zchangelog
.Nd read a dataset's metadata change stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm register
.Ar dataset
.Ar consumer
.Op Ar op,op,...
.Nm
.Cm read
.Ar dataset
.Op Fl c Ar consumer
.Op Fl s Ar seq
.Op Fl n Ar count
.Op Fl w Ar ms
.Op Fl fapj
.Nm
.Cm clear
.Ar dataset
.Ar consumer
.Ar seq
.Nm
.Cm unregister
.Ar dataset
.Ar consumer
.Nm
.Cm status
.Ar dataset
.Op Fl j
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Registers a named consumer, reads metadata change records incrementally
from a cursor, clears processed records and trims the stream.
The stream itself is produced when the dataset property
.Sy changelog
is enabled; see
.Xr zfsprops 7 .
.Pp
A rename produces one record with both names packed as
.Ql old\0new
in the name field and the old parent in the spare field
.Pq Dv CL_F_RENAME2 .
Names longer than 72 bytes are truncated and flagged
.Pq Dv CL_F_NAME_TRUNC .
.Pp
The subcommands:
.Bl -tag -width "unregister"
.It Cm register
Register
.Ar consumer
on
.Ar dataset .
The optional comma-separated op list restricts the consumer's mask to
those operations.
Prints the seq the consumer starts from.
.It Cm read
Read up to
.Fl n
records from the cursor
.Fl s ,
or from the consumer's clear point when
.Fl c
is given.
.Fl w
waits for new records up to
.Ar ms
milliseconds before returning.
.Fl f
follows, reading repeatedly and clearing nothing by itself.
.Fl a
clears up to the returned cursor after each read
.Pq at-least-once delivery .
.Fl p
resolves record objects to paths.
.Fl j
prints one JSON object per record and a trailing
.Ql meta
line with cursor/head/tail/generation.
A gap warning on stderr means records were dropped
(retention exceeded or an async flush lost in a crash);
resync with a full scan.
.It Cm clear
Acknowledge records up to
.Ar seq
for
.Ar consumer .
Records every consumer has acked are freed by trim.
.It Cm unregister
Remove
.Ar consumer .
.It Cm status
Print head, tail, generation and pending record count.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl # Nm zchangelog Cm register Ar tank/data consumer1
.Dl # Nm zchangelog Cm read Ar tank/data Fl c Ar consumer1 Fl a Fl n 512
.Dl # Nm zchangelog Cm read Ar tank/data Fl f Fl j
.Dl # Nm zchangelog Cm clear Ar tank/data Ar consumer1 Ar 1048576
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zfsprops 7 ,
.Xr zfs-diff 8
